  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixConfirm" xml:space="preserve"><value>Queue</value></data>
  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixDetail_Generic" xml:space="preserve"><value>What happens: the selected fix action is queued for each item.
What to expect: some items may improve. Others can stay unchanged if the job fails, finds no data, or is not applicable.</value></data>
  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixDetail_OrphanFile" xml:space="preserve"><value>What happens: queues media creation (RetryCreateMedia) for unlinked files.
What to expect: files that already have identification may attach to a media. Files without identification usually stay unlinked until you re-identify them manually. Create/match failures also leave the file unlinked.</value></data>
  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixDetail_MissingFileMetadata" xml:space="preserve"><value>What happens: queues file metadata extraction (ffprobe / CreateFileMetadatas).
What to expect: most readable files get container metadata. Corrupt, locked, or unsupported files can stay without file metadata.</value></data>
  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixDetail_MissingExternalId" xml:space="preserve"><value>What happens: queues automatic re-identification against metadata providers.
What to expect: some medias may get an external ID. Many can stay unmatched if title/year/provider lookup finds nothing - nothing is forced and the issue can remain.</value></data>
  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixDetail_MissingMetadata" xml:space="preserve"><value>What happens: queues a metadata refresh from providers (works best when an external ID already exists).
What to expect: genres/overview and similar fields may fill when the provider returns data. Empty or partial provider responses leave gaps. Items without a usable identity may not improve.</value></data>
  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixDetail_MissingPictures" xml:space="preserve"><value>What happens: queues a metadata refresh aimed at re-downloading missing artwork.
What to expect: posters/backdrops may appear when the provider has images. If the provider has no art (or refresh fails), pictures can stay missing.</value></data>
  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixDetail_StaleMetadata" xml:space="preserve"><value>What happens: queues a refresh for medias whose metadata is past the library refresh interval.
What to expect: fields update when providers respond. Rate limits, errors, or unchanged remote data can leave items looking stale until a later run.</value></data>
  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixDetail_MissingMembers" xml:space="preserve"><value>What happens: queues a metadata refresh to complete missing artist members/credits.
What to expect: members may fill when the provider returns credits. Incomplete provider data can leave the artist still missing members.</value></data>
  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixDetail_MissingHlsSegments" xml:space="preserve"><value>What happens: queues HLS / keyframe segment computation for eligible video files.
What to expect: keyframe timestamps are stored when probing can read them. If none are reported, one segment covers the whole file from the start (always a valid decode point). Playback transcodes when transmux still cannot use that timeline.</value></data>
  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixDetail_MissingChapters" xml:space="preserve"><value>What happens: queues extraction of embedded file chapters.
What to expect: chapters appear when the file contains chapter atoms. Files without embedded chapters stay without chapters.</value></data>
  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixDetail_MissingThemeSong" xml:space="preserve"><value>What happens: queues theme song generation (and intro detection first when needed).
What to expect: a theme file may be produced when usable intro audio exists. Otherwise the theme can stay missing.</value></data>
  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixDetail_MissingIntroOutro" xml:space="preserve"><value>What happens: queues season-level intro/outro detection.
What to expect: Intro/Outro segments appear when the detector finds a reliable match. Short seasons or weak similarity can yield no segments.</value></data>
  <data name="ConfirmBulkFixDetail_MissingAudioAnalysis" xml:space="preserve"><value>What happens: queues audio analysis (AudioMuse) for music tracks.
What to expect: analysis completes for processable tracks. Failures leave analysis missing.</value></data>
